there is something seductive about order. Even more than power, order tempts.
The reason for this is less human than power's appeal, which is unfortunate for
all the rough edges of the world and beyond. Oh, is that a scuff-mark on the
tile floor of the walmart? Better tear down the entire building just to be sure.

order means that everything is in it's place. All things, in a land of perfect
order, must be working toward some ultimate (or ulterior) goal. This is not
always a good thing, because goals are temporary. What lies behind them? Well,
nobody can say, because nobody is moving aside, getting a better glance at the
stated goal, and it's various trajectories. Sometimes it's better to improve
laterally, rather than force your way through a difficult spot. Why carve a
tunnel through the mountain, when you could wander through the hills a bit and
find your way to the same destination?

